# AgentOS UI primitives

Design philosophy: one shared look across Shell, builtins, and extension UI.

## File naming

Use **kebab-case** for all UI/source files: `activity-bar.tsx`, `home-dashboard.tsx`, `mount.test.tsx`. Keep React component exports in PascalCase (`export function ActivityBar`).

## Default

Import base controls from `@agentos/ui/components/*` (shadcn + Tailwind tokens in `@agentos/ui/globals.css`).

| Need | Use |
| ---- | --- |
| Button / icon button | `@agentos/ui/components/button` |
| Text / textarea | `@agentos/ui/components/input`, `textarea` |
| Checkbox / switch / radio | `checkbox`, `switch`, `radio-group` |
| Select / dropdown / menu | `select`, `dropdown-menu`, `combobox` |
| Dialog / sheet / popover | `dialog`, `sheet`, `popover`, `tooltip` |
| Layout chrome helpers | `separator`, `scroll-area`, `card`, `badge`, `tabs` |
| Class merge | `cn` from `@agentos/ui/lib/utils` |

Icons: `@phosphor-icons/react` (matches the UI package).

Themes: wrap app/Shell with `@agentos/ui/components/theme-provider` (`next-themes`). Default is `dark`; extend `AGENTOS_THEMES` when adding themes. Do not hardcode a `dark` class on layout roots.

## Do not

- Do **not** use native `<button>`, `<input>`, `<textarea>`, `<select>`, `<option>`, or hand-rolled checkbox/radio markup when an `@agentos/ui` component exists.
- Do **not** invent parallel button/input styles or one-off CSS that bypasses design tokens.
- Do **not** import another component library for base controls.

## Exceptions (native HTML OK)

Only when specifically required, for example:

- Semantic landmarks / structure: `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<aside>`, `<footer>`, `<section>`, `<form>`
- Hidden iframe parks / slot hosts (`data-slot=…`)
- File inputs or other controls with no shadcn equivalent yet
- Non-UI host glue (tests, SSR string checks)

When in doubt, prefer `@agentos/ui` and ask before adding a new primitive package.
